|diced]] [[Cookbook:Onion|onions]]\n*½ tablespoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n*2 cloves [[Cookbook:Mince|minced]] [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]]\n*1 dash [[Cookbook:Red Pepper|red pepper]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Pound|pound]] [[Cookbook:Ground Beef|ground beef substitute]] (e.g. MorningStar Farms Grillers Recipe Crumbles)\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n*8 [[Cookbook:Tortilla|flour tortillas]]\n\n=== Suggested toppings ===\n*1 can [[Cookbook:Refried Beans|refried beans]]\n*1 [[Cookbook:Tomato|tomato]], chopped\n*1 cup chopped [[Cookbook:Onion|onion]]\n*2 cups shredded [[Cookbook:Lettuce|lettuce]]\n*1 cup shredded Colby-Jack [[Cookbook:Cheese|cheese]] (or [[Cookbook:Cheddar Cheese|cheddar]])\n*[[Cookbook:Sour Cream|sour cream]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#In a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] brown onions on medium-low heat.\n#Add garlic, chilli powder, paprika, salt, and red pepper. Stir and cook for 1 minute.\n#Add beef substitute and water. Cook for 10–15 minutes until most of the water is gone.\n#Meanwhile [[Cookbook:Chopping|chop]] and shred the toppings as needed. Put toppings in bowls on table.\n#Start to warm refried beans in a small pot.\n#Heat another [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] on medium-low heat.\n#Put vegetarian taco meat and refried beans in bowls and place on table.\n#Put floured tortilla in pan and lightly brown both sides. As tortillas are ready allow guests to select their own toppings.\n\n== Notes, tips, and variations ==\n\n* The filling and refried beans keep well in the refrigerator.\n\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Southwestern recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using meat substitutes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for tacos]]\n[[Category:Recipes using monterey jack]]\n[[Category:Colby recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cheddar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using lettuce]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Vegetarian Soft Tacos","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 